I got my first 3.1.x ascension (on 3.1.1, to be exact) today...  Playing a
caveman, too...  Here are some comments:

1.	The Chromatic Dragon is tough indeed.  Although I had a +7 Vorpal
	Blade (from a bones file), it was able to take me down to 8 HP while
	it still had about a third left.  I prayed, and was lucky enough to
	get a favorable response from Anu (I wasn't exactly sure about that
	being the right way to do, given that Claudius the Pioneer was the
	Hand of Elbereth), and later on was able to cut the head off the
	Dragon.

2.	Two magic lamps early made it relatively easy through the castle.
	Other than the wand of wishing that was at the castle, I also got
	another one on the Sanctum level, and that wand had one wish left by
	the time that I sacrificed the Amulet.

3.	With the +7 Vorpal Blade (and +6 Scepter of Might as a backup), and
	with a good complement of armor (crystal plate mail, +5 cloak of
	magic resistance, +3 gauntlets of power, +4 shield of reflection,
	+3 speed boots), Gehennom was basically a piece of cake, on the way
	down.  Two blessed spellbooks of magic mapping made finding Vlad's
	Tower (which I had found difficult the last time I was able to go this
	deep) trivial.

4.	The High Priest of Moloch is too easy...  He should have more good
	items/spells with which to fight.  Maybe Moloch himself should show up
	if you dispatch the high priest?

5.	Something I hated, on the way up, was (as many others have commented)
	the thing where you get bounced down a level or two occasionally.  It
	was particularly unbearable when you get bumped down to a non-teleport
	level...

6.	Unlike what I've heard before, the Medusa didn't come back when I came
	back up; was that an incorrect information?

7.	Load up on wands of digging on the way up!  You'll need them on the
	Earth Elemental level...  (Although I also had the option of
	polymorphing into a xorn, but thought that as too dangerous.)

8.	Finding the magic portals in the end level was not that difficult;
	but I ended up using a wish to get a blessed crystal ball anyway...

9.	I forgot to get rid of conflict (given by invoking the Scepter of
	Might, which otherwise is pretty worthless, IMO), before reaching the
	Astral level, and the angels were not very pleased with that, but I
	didn't have much problem getting them to kill each other anyway.  The
	one demigod that I encountered was indeed a wimp, as others have
	remarked.

10.	By the time I got into the temple of Anu, the High Priest of Anu was
	already dead (killed by a jabberwock), but I think I still got the
	"Pilgrim, you enter a holy place" message...  If that is correct (I
	am not totally sure that the priest was killed before I entered the
	temple) then that is possibly a bug.

11.	Judging from the fact that the priest was killed by a jabberwock,
	although I didn't run into the other two high priests, I would assume
	that they would be too easy to kill as well.

Probably won't play for a few more days, for now...

